response:
 The given sequence is $$
\frac23, \frac34, \frac45, \frac56, \dots
$$. To find the product of the first 20 terms, we can write the sequence as $$
\frac23, \frac34, \frac45, \frac56, \dots, \frac{19}{20}
$$. The product of these terms is $$\frac23 \times \frac34 \times \frac45 \times \frac56 \times \dots \times \frac{19}{20} = \frac{2 \times 3 \times 4 \times 5 \times \dots \times 19}{3 \times 4 \times 5 \times 6 \times \dots \times 20}
$$. Notice that in the numerator and the denominator, most terms cancel out, leaving us with $$\frac{2}{20} = \frac{1}{10}$$. </think> <answer> $\frac{1}{10}$ </answer>

